# Go backend ignores.
#
# NOTE ON ANCHORING: this file also governs backend/ml (the Python workspace),
# because gitignore rules apply to every subdirectory. Rules that describe *this
# module's* build output are therefore anchored with a leading slash, so they
# match only at backend/ and cannot silently swallow an ml/ file that happens to
# share a name. Rules that should apply everywhere (secrets, OS noise) stay
# unanchored on purpose. ml/ has its own .gitignore for its own artefacts.

# Binaries — /bin is this module's build output; an ml/bin/ would be unrelated.
/bin/
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary
*.test

# Go coverage output. Anchored: an unanchored *.out would also hide evaluation
# reports written under ml/data, which are worth reviewing in a diff.
/coverage.out
/coverage.html

# Go workspace
go.work
go.work.sum

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environment — unanchored on purpose: a stray .env must never be committed,
# wherever it appears. The checked-in template is the documented exception.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# Vendor (optional)
# vendor/

# Build output — anchored; ml/ declares its own dist/ and build/ rules.
/dist/
/tmp/
/.tmp/

# Air hot-reload
/bin/air
